---
// Applicant privacy notice — STUB. Route authorised by ROUTE-CONTRACT
// Amendment 05 (owner decision 2026-09-26: build the player application
// form, docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-26-join-form-design.md).
//
// Why a stub and not a policy: the form's only outbound path is
// `submitForm(payload)`, whose v1 adapter answers `unavailable` and
// discards the payload (FORM-CONTRACT, FROZEN). No applicant data is
// transmitted, so there is no live handling to describe, no retention
// promise that can be kept and no lawful basis to assert. Those terms
// belong to the club and are UNKNOWN until online applications open — the
// working notice ships then. Inventing a retention period, a data-
// protection contact or a complaints route here would be a fabricated
// legal claim, so this page states only what the form asks for and which
// channels are real (CLAUDE.md: UNKNOWN stays UNKNOWN).
//
// `noindex` follows the repo's convention for shell pages
// (ROUTE-CONTRACT Amendment 01 condition 2; `/services`, `/membership`,
// `/join`, `/offline` all ship it): a stub is not public content, and
// indexing an incomplete notice would invite readers to treat it as the
// club's policy. It flips to indexable only when the working notice
// replaces this text.
//
// One small scoped rule below (the list reset): the base type grammar
// styles paragraphs but leaves browser-default bullets, which read as
// stray marks on these short channel lists. Tokens-only, no new tokens.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import PageBanner from '../components/PageBanner.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { socialDisplayName } from '../components/SocialLinks.astro';
import { contact, homepage } from '../content/homepage-data';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Notice — UK Bangla Tigers"
  description="What the UK Bangla Tigers application form asks for, and what is not settled yet."
  noindex={true}
>
  <Header nav={homepage.nav} cta={homepage.primaryCta} />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <PageBanner
      title="Privacy Notice"
      crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy Notice' }]}
    />

    <Section>
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="Privacy" heading="What This Notice Is" />
      <p>
        This page is a placeholder, not a privacy policy. It is published ahead of online
        applications so the application form has something honest to point at. While online
        applications are closed, the form on the
        <a href="/join/">Join the Club</a> page sends nothing and stores nothing: what you type
        is checked in your own browser and then discarded. The working notice — the one an
        applicant can rely on — is published when online applications open.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section surface="alt">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="The Form" heading="Details the Form Asks For" />
      <p>When online applications open, the form asks for:</p>
      <ul class="ukbt-privacy-list">
        <li>Full name</li>
        <li>Date of birth</li>
        <li>Nationality</li>
        <li>Country of residency</li>
        <li>Phone number</li>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>A link to your main cricket statistics profile (optional)</li>
        <li>Links to your cricket videos (optional)</li>
        <li>A photograph (optional; uploads open with online applications)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        That is the whole list — the form asks for nothing else. An exact date of birth is
        asked for, rather than an age band, because the club develops young players as well as
        playing adult cricket. Photo upload stays switched off until applications open, so no
        picture can be sent through the form today.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section>
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="Unknown" heading="What Is Not Settled Yet" />
      <p>
        This notice does not state a retention period, a lawful basis, a data-protection contact
        or a complaints route. None of those is decided yet, and none is invented here. They are
        the club's to set, and they are written out in full in the working notice that ships with
        online applications. Until then, read this page as a plain description of what the form
        asks for, and nothing more.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section surface="alt" paddingBottom="normal">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="Contact" heading="Reaching the Club" />
      <p>
        If you have a question about your details, or want to ask what the club holds about you
        today, use a channel that is already working:
      </p>
      <ul class="ukbt-privacy-list">
        <li>
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          Phone: <a href={contact.phoneHref}>{contact.phoneDisplay}</a>
        </li>
        {
          homepage.social.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <a href={s.url} rel="me noopener">{socialDisplayName(s.platform)}</a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </Section>
  </main>
  <Footer social={homepage.social} nav={homepage.nav} secondaryNav={homepage.secondaryNav} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Intended-list reset: no browser bullets, no UA indent, paragraph-rhythm
     bottom margin (the same token base type uses) and an even token gap —
     so each channel reads as a designed item, not a default list. */
  .ukbt-privacy-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 var(--ukbt-font-body-paragraph-margin-bottom) 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--ukbt-space-2);
  }
</style>
